# Imported INSIDE the {$SITE_DOMAIN} site block, production only.
#
# Mail lives at mail.tatvaos.com and nowhere else. Both hostnames are front
# doors onto the same web container, so without this every product answered on
# every host — core.tatvaos.com/mail/inbox served the app on the wrong domain.
#
# WHY A handle, NOT A BARE redir. A bare `redir` sits outside the site's
# `handle` blocks, and Caddy's directive ordering let the catch-all
# `handle { reverse_proxy web:3000 }` win first — so the redirect never fired
# and the page 200'd. Wrapping it in a `handle` puts it in the same mutually-
# exclusive group as that catch-all; because this fragment is imported before
# the other handles, it is matched first for /mail paths and redirects
# deterministically. The path is preserved ({uri}) and the auth cookie is on
# .tatvaos.com, so a deep link and the session both survive the hop.
handle /mail /mail/* {
    redir https://{$MAIL_DOMAIN}{uri} 302
}
